# Force LF everywhere. This matters most for setup.sh: if it ever gets
# saved/committed with Windows-style CRLF line endings, bash on Mac/Linux
# (and Git Bash/WSL on Windows) will fail with cryptic errors like
# "$'\r': command not found" or "bad interpreter". Forcing LF in the repo
# means everyone's checkout is consistent regardless of what OS they're on.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
